 75GE c  2012Me04 (also 2010Me01): E(n)(average)=0.00183 eV, cold neutrons from 
 75GE2c  reactor at PGAA research reactor facility in Garching. Measured E|g,   
 75GE3c  I|g, |g|g coin using two Compton suppressed HPGe detectors. Sample was 
 75GE4c  enriched to 39.2% in {+74}Ge. 2010Me01 and 2009Me06 from the same      
 75GE5c  group, who reported capture cross sections for the isomeric state      
 75GE6c  and g.s.                                                               
 75GE c  2011Ha56: cold neutrons from JRR-3 reactor at JAEA facility. Measured  
 75GE2c  E|g, I|g, |g|g coin using STELLA array of eight clover Ge detectors    
 75GE3c  with BGO Compton suppressors. Full details of this study are not       
 75GE4c  yet available                                                          
 75GE c  Other |g-ray studies:                                                  
 75GE c  1972Gr34, 1972Ha74, 1972We10: measured E|g, absolute I|g, S(n)         
 75GE c  1991Is01: measured E|g, absolute I|g (only primary transitions were    
 75GE2c  reported), deduced S(n)                                                
 75GE c  Cross section and other measurements:                                  
 75GE c  2009Ma35: measured |s in (n,|g) by activation; E(n)=25 keV             
 75GE c  2007ChZX: PGAA database. In the elemental cross section measurements,  
 75GE2c  8 primary |g rays and 13 secondary gamma rays were assigned to {+75}Ge.
 75GE c  1987Ko23: measured coherent scattering lengths, |s                     
 75GE c  1987Li05: non statistical effects in (n,|g); calculated |s(E)          
 75GE c  1979An22: measured |s in (n,|g); E(n)=25 keV                           
 75GE D  1977Ba13: non-statistical effects in (N,G)                             
 75GE c  1972La15: measured isomeric cross-section ratios in (n,|g) at          
 75GE2c  E(n)=25 {I5} keV                                                       
 75GE c  1970Di03: |s(n,|g) at E(n)=3 MeV                                       
 75GE c  1969Pr08, 1968Ma12, 1967Ok01 (isomer cross section)                    
